📘 Load Balancer Advanced Concepts — Quick Notes
1️⃣ Reverse Proxy
✅ Definition
A reverse proxy sits in front of backend servers and forwards requests.

Client → Reverse Proxy → Server
✅ Key Points
Client never sees actual servers
Improves security + performance
Used by Load Balancers (L7)
✅ Use Cases
Routing
Caching
Authentication
🧠 Analogy: Receptionist directing visitors

2️⃣ Sticky Sessions (Session Affinity)
✅ Definition
Ensures a user always hits the same server

User → Server A → Server A → Server A
✅ How
Cookie-based
IP-based
✅ Problem it solves
Keeps session data consistent
⚠️ Drawbacks
Poor load balancing
Hard to scale
✅ Better:

Use Redis / DB session store
3️⃣ SSL Termination
✅ Definition
Load Balancer handles HTTPS encryption/decryption

Client (HTTPS)
    ↓
LB (decrypt)
    ↓
Server (HTTP)
✅ Benefits
Faster backend
Easy certificate management
Centralized security
✅ Types
Termination ✅ (common)
Passthrough
End-to-end SSL
4️⃣ HA / Failover (High Availability)
✅ Goal
Avoid downtime if LB/server fails

✅ Approaches
🔹 Active-Passive
Primary LB → Backup LB (standby)
🔹 Active-Active
LB1 + LB2 both serving traffic
✅ Tools
DNS failover
Cloud LB (AWS ELB)
5️⃣ Global Load Balancing
✅ Definition
Routes users to nearest/geographically optimal region

India → Mumbai region  
US → Virginia region
✅ Techniques
Geo-based routing
Latency-based routing
Failover routing
✅ Tools
Route53
Cloudflare
6️⃣ Advanced Algorithms
✅ Basic
Round Robin
Least Connections
Text type
l4loadbalancer
✅ Advanced
🔹 Weighted Round Robin
Different traffic weights
🔹 Least Response Time
Fastest server wins
🔹 Consistent Hashing
Same user → same server
🔹 IP Hash
Based on client IP
Text type
l4loadbalancer
7️⃣ Health Checks (Deep)
✅ Purpose
Ensure traffic goes only to healthy servers
Text type
l4loadbalancer

✅ Types
🔹 L4 Health Check
TCP connection test
🔹 L7 Health Check
HTTP endpoint:
GET /health → 200 OK
✅ Advanced Settings
Retry count (e.g., 3 failures)
Timeout
Interval
✅ Behavior
Server fails 3 times → marked unhealthy
8️⃣ Rate Limiting
✅ Definition
Limits number of requests per user/IP

100 requests/minute/user
✅ Why
Prevent abuse (DDoS)
Protect backend
Fair usage
✅ Algorithms
🔹 Token Bucket
Tokens refill over time
🔹 Leaky Bucket
Fixed output rate
🔹 Sliding Window
Time-based counting
✅ Applied At
API Gateway
L7 Load Balancer
🧠 Final Cheat Sheet (1-Min Revision)
Reverse Proxy → Entry layer, hides servers
Sticky Session → Same user → same server
SSL Termination → LB handles HTTPS
HA/Failover → Multiple LBs avoid downtime
Global LB → Route by region/latency
Algorithms → RR, Least Conn, Hashing
Health Checks → Remove unhealthy servers
Rate Limiting → Control request volume
